{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator instance structure blender operator instance structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Instance Structure","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender PointerRNA","Blender Non-Modal Operator","Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator instance structure blender operator instance structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Instance Structure","heading":"Blender Operator Instance Structure","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`wmOperator` is the record for one occurrence of an operation. It stores the type identifier, a runtime pointer to the [[Blender Operator Type Structure]], a [[Blender PointerRNA]] containing the current property values, linked-list navigation, and data needed while the operation is being processed.\n\nBecause the record is defined in Blender DNA, operator-stack information can be persistent even though callback pointers are resolved at runtime. A [[Blender Non-Modal Operator]] may need it only for one execution, while a [[Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle]] retains instance state across repeated events.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender PointerRNA","Blender Non-Modal Operator","Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator instance structure blender operator instance structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Instance Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Instance Structure","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender PointerRNA","Blender Non-Modal Operator","Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}